ListNode leftRotate(ListNode head) {
/* General idea being, last element needs to point to head and head should be disconnected from its next element */

/* Hold on to the original head */
temp = head;

/* We will have to return the new head so hold on to it as well */
head = head->next;

/* Point (X): Disconnect the original head */
temp->next = null;

/* Traverse until we find the last element */
node = head;
prev = null;
while (node) {
   prev = node;
   node = node->next;
}

/* Connect last element to the old head */
prev->next = temp;

/* Return the new head */
return head;
}


For rightRotate, its the same program as above except remove Point (X) and return prev instead of head

